0). \r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:4690","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":27596,"name":"Vibraphonic"},{"active":true,"id":29518,"name":"Brooklyn Funk Essentials"},{"active":false,"id":60232,"name":"This Mortal Coil"},{"active":true,"id":337255,"name":"Powerbass"},{"active":false,"id":3399670,"name":"Grand Union Orchestra"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["A.  Limerick","A. Limerick","A.Limerick","A.T. Limerick","Alison","Alison Lemerick","Alison Limerik","Alison Limmerick","Alison Therese","Alison Therese Limerick","Alison Therse Limerick","Alison Thérèse Limerick","Allison Limerick","Limerick","Limerick Alison","Limerick Allison","Limerik","艾莉森琳芮克"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4690-Alison-Limerick","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.facebook.com/alisonlimeric","http://www.facebook.com/alisonlimerick1","http://www.instagram.com/alison_limerick","http://www.soundcloud.com/alison-limerick","http://twitter.com/alisonlimerick1","http://www.youtube.com/user/AlisonLimerickVEVO","","http://www.youtube.com/@AlisonLimerickOfficial"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/7272502/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"7272502","image":"https://i.discogs.com/5hWBfc1QJFySFiLMeNaZJCgVO7TmSfVCA3ejIEuhSFk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:396/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTcyNzI1/MDItMTYzNTI2MDQ4/Ni0xNzM4LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/vZZoGm9RWsg0nXARiqJ5shshhJv7VRkSr2Gt960_1tY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTcyNzI1/MDItMTYzNTI2MDQ4/Ni0xNzM4LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Alyssa Michelle Stephens (born December 22, 1998), known professionally as Mulatto, is an American rapper. She is known for being the inaugural winner of the Lifetime reality series The Rap Game. Mulatto's breakthrough occurred with her 2019 single, \"Bitch from da Souf\", and consequently she signed to [l=RCA Records].\r\n\r\nMulatto changed her stage name to \"[a10439215]\" in January 2021 and has since then released all of her music under her new stage name.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:7272502","relations":{"aliases":[{"id":6141129,"name":"Miss Mulatto"},{"id":9608326,"name":"Alyssa Stephens"},{"id":10439215,"name":"Latto"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Latto"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/7272502-Mulatto-2","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/missmulatto247"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/72965/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"72965","image":"https://i.discogs.com/LqUG7g5rTbcS8780vgdVNc93JCmKNy5L4cVX9jfRn_8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:451/w:300/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTcyOTY1/LTExMDc4OTQyNDQu/anBn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/zLH5XULWjiOMAsXm90EybsapMycAqbE2m9VAsnTPscE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTcyOTY1/LTExMDc4OTQyNDQu/anBn.jpeg","profile":"She holds the distinction of being the first Filipino American to make it in the mainstream music industry. Dubbed as the new \"Queen of Freestyle\", Enriquez was the first artist to be signed by Classified Records, a Filipino-owned recording company when it was established in 1993.\r\n\r\n\r\nWhen Enriquez's first single became a success, larger recording companies began to take notice. Born and raised in San Francisco, California, Jocelyn Enriquez is the daughter of Filipino parents from Manila and the province of Pangasinan. \r\n\r\n\r\nBy late April 1997, Enriquez's first single \"Do You Miss Me?\" had placed 49th on the Billboard Top 100 singles chart, 7th in Singapore, and among the top 20 in Canada. Then she had the hit song, \"A Little Bit of Ecstasy\". By August 1997. every day in New York City, one could hear \"Do You Miss Me?\" or \"A Little Bit of Ecstasy\".\r\n\r\n\r\nAs a teenager, she became involved in a community outreach program called the Young Filipino Entertainers' Club. From that time on, there was no turning back for Enriquez. The break that she was waiting for came when she first signed with the Bay-area based Classified Records. \r\n\r\n\r\nIt was Glenn Gutierrez, a Filipino American producer and composer, who convinced her to try dance music. She tried it. \"I've Been Thinking About You\" became a hit and it led to an album. Two years later, she had two songs on the charts.\r\n\r\nNow, a truly successful music career awaits this Filipino American artist. She, however, is no longer connected with Classified Records, but with another recording company that earlier merged with and then separated from Classified Records.\r\n\r\nJocelyn went back full force in 2003 with her comeback third album All My Life released by her own record label JEM Entertainment. This album features all kinds of dance music elements including the album single \"All My Life\" written by DJ Sammy which full of trance feeling, then follows with the single \"No Way No How\" and \"Why\".\r\n\r\nShortly after her third album was released, she decided to settle down in San Antonio, Texas and spend time with her husband Alain Macasadia and her four kids as a full-time mother and wife being Mrs. Jocelyn E. Macasadia. She turned down all of the requests being offered just to come back as an old diva. \r\n\r\nSurprisingly, after her years of hiatus she's back in the music scene in 2018 performing again live on stage in some various places in the U.S. with her come back single \"To Love Again\". She also recorded her 2020 version of her classic ballad hit \"You Are The One\". Currently she released a single \"Beauty Comes Through Pain\" which later on the remixes were released.\r\n","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:72965","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":41798,"name":"Stars On 54"},{"active":false,"id":437790,"name":"Pinay"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["J. Enriquez","J.Enriquez","Jacelyn Enriques","Jocelyn","Jocelyn Enrique","Jocelyn Enriques","Jocelyn Enriqurz","Jocelyn Henriquez","Joselyn Enrique